{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Lodge here tonight.</b> The holy spirit does not rest upon him except at night — and so for all the prophets of the nations of the world. And so Lavan — in a dream of the night, as it says (Genesis 31) ״וַיָּבֹא אֱלֹהִים אֶל לָבָן הָאֲרַמִּי בַּחֲלֹם הַלַּיְלָה״ — like a man who goes to his concubine in secret (Tanchuma; Vayikra Rabbah 1)." "<b>As YHWH will speak to me.</b> If He permits me to go with men such as you, I will go with you — perhaps it is not His glory to let me go except with officers greater than you." "<b>And they stayed.</b> A term of delay."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:12:10.001088966Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}